<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abu al-Hasan Ali of Granada</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1485">1485</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Muley Hacén</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abu al-Hasan Ali, known to the Castilians as Muley Hacén, was Nasrid emir of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/granada">Granada</a> from 1464 to 1482 and again in 1483–1485. His seizure of the Castilian town of Zahara in 1481 provoked the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/granada-war">Granada War</a>. Weakened by the revolt of his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-xii-of-granada">Boabdil</a> and by court rivalries, he gave up power to his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-xiii-of-granada">Muhammad al-Zaghal</a> and died in 1485.</p></div>
